# Project Wiki ↔ Roadmap Sync

## File roles

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `PROJECT_WIKI.md` | Source of truth — direction, context, full checklists |
| `content/roadmap/roadmap.md` | Public summary — concise checklists only (rendered at `/roadmap`) |

## When editing either file

1. **Plan or complete a task** → update `PROJECT_WIKI.md` first (Checklists + Current State)
2. **Sync to roadmap** → copy the matching checklist section to `content/roadmap/roadmap.md`
3. **Keep roadmap scannable** — no long rationale, architecture notes, or internal-only items
4. **Mark `[x]` in both** when a public-facing item is done

## What stays wiki-only (do NOT add to roadmap)

- `English` checklist (managed personally by the maintainer)
- Infrastructure & DX (README, deployment, SEO)
- Notes for AI Assistants, English Learning Strategy, Architecture
- Done / in-progress narrative in Current State

## Section mapping

Roadmap groups sections under two `#` headings; wiki uses flat `### Group — Section` names:

- Wiki `Menu — Log` → roadmap `## Log` under `# Menu`
- Wiki `Menu — Portfolio` → roadmap `## Portfolio` under `# Menu`
- Wiki `Menu — About` → roadmap `## About` under `# Menu`
- Wiki `UI — Anchors` → roadmap `## Anchors` under `# UI`
- Wiki `UI — Responsive` → roadmap `## Responsive` under `# UI`
- Wiki `UI — Dark Mode` → roadmap `## Dark Mode` under `# UI`

**Roadmap structure**: `# Menu` (Log, Portfolio, About) → `# UI` (Anchors, Responsive, Dark Mode).

## Before finishing a task that touches planning

- [ ] Wiki checklist reflects the change
- [ ] Roadmap has the matching public items
- [ ] Wiki `Current State` updated if milestone-level progress changed
